-- Vector Golf Performance · Package 7E.4.2 complete golf-drill instructions
-- Generated from the 224 coded routes in Performance Engine v3.1. No drill codes or diagnostic links are changed.
update public.library_items as item set
  setup=content.setup,
  instructions=content.instructions,
  intention=content.intention,
  equipment=content.equipment,
  progression=content.progression,
  regression=content.regression,
  updated_at=now()
from (values
('DR-3A-01','Choose one clear target and place an alignment stick parallel to it. Use a mid-iron and create two columns on a record sheet: start direction and curve direction.','1. Hit the first ball with a normal swing.
2. Call the initial start direction before judging curve.
3. Call the curve direction separately, then record both.
4. Repeat without changing technique until the full set is classified.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes club path most predictably.','Alignment stick; target; shot-record sheet or launch monitor when available','Predict the result before viewing feedback, then repeat the test with a different club or target while preserving shot order.','Use one club, one target and two groups of three balls with the record sheet completed immediately after each shot.'),
('DR-3A-02','Aim at one fixed target with alignment verified. Use the same club and intention for every shot, and prepare a numbered record for club path, strike and ball flight.','1. Hit the baseline balls with one target and normal intent.
2. After each ball, record face/start, path/curve and strike rather than relying on the average.
3. Mark repeated clusters and the largest costly miss.
4. Hit the confirmation set while changing only the variable selected by the coach.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes club path most predictably.','Alignment stick; target; shot-record sheet or launch monitor when available','Predict the result before viewing feedback, then repeat the test with a different club or target while preserving shot order.','Use one club, one target and two groups of three balls with the record sheet completed immediately after each shot.'),
('DR-3A-03','Set one centre target plus reference targets either side. Begin with a mid-iron and identify the leftward or less rightward window required for each ball.','1. Hit one baseline ball.
2. Make an exaggerated rehearsal sending the club path leftward or less rightward.
3. Hit the paired ball with the same exaggerated intention.
4. Finish with neutral-intention balls and compare them with baseline.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Predict the result before viewing feedback, then repeat the test with a different club or target while preserving shot order.','Use one club, one target and two groups of three balls with the record sheet completed immediately after each shot.'),
('DR-3A-04','Apply impact spray or tape to the clubface. Use one target, one club and a numbered shot record so strike location can be matched to each flight.','1. Hit each ball and mark its face-strike location before the next shot.
2. Record start, curve and the measured delivery variable.
3. Compare heel, centre and toe groups rather than isolated shots.
4. Finish by returning strike to the centre without changing the intended target.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes club path most predictably.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Predict the result before viewing feedback, then repeat the test with a different club or target while preserving shot order.','Use one club, one target and two groups of three balls with the record sheet completed immediately after each shot.'),
('DR-3A-05','Place one stick on the target line beyond the ball and a second parallel to it beside the toes. Set the clubface first, then build feet, knees, hips and shoulders around the verified line.','1. Stand behind the ball and choose the exact start line.
2. Set the clubface to that line before placing the feet.
3. Match the body to the parallel reference and hit the shot.
4. Step away completely and rebuild the station for every repetition.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-06','Lay an alignment stick across the toe line and mark back, normal and forward ball positions one ball-width apart. Keep stance width and target constant.','1. Hit the first set from the back marker, the second from normal and the third from forward.
2. Keep target, stance width and swing intention unchanged.
3. Record strike, start, curve and ground contact for every ball.
4. Return to the best position for the consolidation set.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Alignment stick; three ball-position markers; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-07','Create low, normal and high tee stations with the same target and ball position. Use impact spray on the driver face and record attack, path and strike when available.','1. Hit equal sets from low, normal and high tees.
2. Keep target and swing intention unchanged.
3. Record face strike, launch, attack and path for each height.
4. Return to the height producing the best combined strike and flight and repeat it.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes club path most predictably.','Driver; three tee heights; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-08','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate leftward or less rightward of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Make three slow takeaways, moving the club through the marked channel.
2. Stop when the shaft is approximately parallel to the ground and check the clubhead/hand relationship.
3. Hit a short shot while missing the reference and preserving the same early direction.
4. Alternate rehearsal and ball until the task survives without looking at the marker.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-09','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Make three slow takeaways, moving the club through the marked channel.
2. Stop when the shaft is approximately parallel to the ground and check the clubhead/hand relationship.
3. Hit a short shot while missing the reference and preserving the same early direction.
4. Alternate rehearsal and ball until the task survives without looking at the marker.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-10','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Place the club at address and soften the arms.
2. Start the chest, arms and club together until the hands reach trail-thigh height.
3. Pause, check that spacing has not collapsed, then complete a three-quarter swing.
4. Blend the pause out while retaining the connected start.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-11','Stand in golf posture with the trail side close enough to a wall or upright reference for the hands or club to approach it during a slow rehearsal without striking it.','1. Rehearse to the top slowly using the wall as the depth reference.
2. Pause and note where the hands finish relative to it.
3. Step into the hitting station and reproduce that depth with a three-quarter shot.
4. Compare the original and adjusted depth while monitoring club path.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Wall or upright reference; mid-iron; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-12','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Hit one normal-length baseline shot.
2. Rehearse a backswing that stops when the lead arm is approximately parallel to the ground.
3. Hit the paired shorter swing with normal through-swing intention.
4. Alternate lengths, then finish with the length producing the best combined result.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes club path most predictably.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-13','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Swing to the top and pause for a clear count of one.
2. During the pause, organise the club and hands toward the selected leftward or less rightward delivery window.
3. Complete the swing at three-quarter speed.
4. Reduce the pause gradually while keeping the same delivery.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-14','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Swing to the top, then rehearse down to the delivery position three times without hitting.
2. Each pump should place the hands, shaft and clubhead in the selected leftward or less rightward corridor.
3. On the third return to the top, swing through and hit the ball.
4. Progress to one pump, then a continuous swing.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-15','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Separate the hands on the grip by approximately one hand-width.
2. Make waist-high rehearsals and feel the hands organise the handle, face and radius together.
3. Hit the split-hand balls at half speed.
4. Return to a normal grip and retain the same delivery relationship.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-16','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate leftward or less rightward of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Rehearse the hands through the marked delivery corridor without a ball.
2. Hit a half shot while the hands pass between the references and the clubhead remains free.
3. Record gate contact, strike and club path.
4. Widen or remove one reference for the final transfer set.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-17','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Aim the clubface at the target, then set the feet and body left of it.
2. Make a waist-high rehearsal following the body line.
3. Hit a half shot with the same motion and balanced finish.
4. Return the stance halfway toward square, then square, while retaining the delivery change.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-18','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Make a half backswing and pause.
2. Rehearse the chest and trail shoulder continuing through the selected leftward or less rightward window.
3. Hit a half shot and hold the finish for two seconds.
4. Increase to three-quarter length only when strike and direction remain functional.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-19','Place a small marker beside each foot so stance width can be rebuilt. Start with feet close enough to make the step or pressure shift obvious and use a short iron.','1. Begin with the feet close together or the trail foot on its marked start point.
2. Start the backswing, then make the prescribed step as the direction changes.
3. Let the step organise pressure and rotation before the arms accelerate.
4. Hit the ball and finish balanced, then blend the motion into a normal stance.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Club; balls; one foot-position marker','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-3A-20','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Apply face spray and hit balls at controlled speed.
2. Check and mark strike after every ball.
3. Do not change the delivery variable until the required centre-strike count is reached.
4. Add the direction or low-point task while continuing to record strike.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-21','Apply impact spray or tape to the clubface. Use one target, one club and a numbered shot record so strike location can be matched to each flight.','1. Hit each ball and mark its face-strike location before the next shot.
2. Record start, curve and the measured delivery variable.
3. Compare heel, centre and toe groups rather than isolated shots.
4. Finish by returning strike to the centre without changing the intended target.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-22','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate leftward or less rightward of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Rehearse through the gate without a ball and identify the centre of the available space.
2. Hit at half speed without contacting either side.
3. Record gate success, strike and ball flight.
4. Narrow the gate slightly or remove one side for transfer; do not chase a perfect zero value.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-23','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Swing until the lead arm is approximately parallel to the ground.
2. Turn through to a matching waist-high finish with steady rhythm.
3. Hold the finish and check strike, start and curve.
4. Build consecutive successful shots before increasing length.','Feel the club and body organise a leftward or less rightward club path pattern without adding effort or steering the ball.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-24','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate leftward or less rightward of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Place two references beyond the ball to show the selected leftward or less rightward exit corridor.
2. Rehearse the clubhead and hands moving through that space after impact.
3. Hit half shots and finish with the club inside the corridor.
4. Remove the nearer reference for the transfer set.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-25','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate leftward or less rightward of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Place the ball on the ground line and identify the target-side contact zone.
2. Hit a three-quarter shot, then mark where the divot or brush began.
3. Record ball contact, strike and direction together.
4. Reset the surface reference and repeat without moving the ball to chase the previous mark.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-3A-26','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Treat three consecutive balls as one set.
2. Rebuild the setup and task before every ball.
3. Score the set only after all three outcomes are known.
4. Restart the streak after a miss and continue until the stated success criterion is achieved.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional club path under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Alignment stick; target; shot-record sheet or launch monitor when available','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-3A-27','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Choose the required start and curve for each ball before addressing it.
2. Build alignment, then make one rehearsal matching face and path to that shape.
3. Hit the shot and score start, curve and strike separately.
4. Randomise the requested shape for the next ball.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional club path under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Alignment stick; target; shot-record sheet or launch monitor when available','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-3A-28','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Begin at roughly 60% effort and hit three balls.
2. Increase effort by about 10% only when club path and strike remain in the task window.
3. Drop back one level immediately when the pattern breaks.
4. Record the highest speed completed twice with a functional pattern.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional club path under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Alignment stick; target; shot-record sheet or launch monitor when available','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-3A-29','Choose three targets with clearly different directions. Place one alignment reference at the hitting area but rebuild the body and face alignment for every shot.','1. Select a different target before each ball.
2. Walk behind the ball, choose the start line and rebuild alignment from the beginning.
3. Make one task-specific rehearsal, then hit.
4. Score the outcome and move to a new target without correcting the previous shot mechanically.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional club path under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-3A-30','Choose one driver target and one iron target. Place both clubs behind the hitting area and keep the alignment reference visible while switching clubs.','1. Hit one ball with the iron task and record it.
2. Change target, select the driver and rebuild its ball position and alignment.
3. Continue alternating clubs without practice balls between them.
4. Score each club against its own strike and flight window.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional club path under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Mid-iron; balls; alignment stick; clear target','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-3A-31','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the club path task to be recognised.','1. Mark a scoring corridor and one prohibited side.
