4. Finish by returning strike to the centre without changing the intended target.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes strike and low point most predictably.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Predict the result before viewing feedback, then repeat the test with a different club or target while preserving shot order.','Use one club, one target and two groups of three balls with the record sheet completed immediately after each shot.'),
('DR-5-05','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Address the ground line without a ball.
2. Make a small swing and brush the surface on the target side of the line.
3. Repeat until the brush begins in the same zone.
4. Place a ball on the line and reproduce the brush while striking the ball first.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-06','Lay an alignment stick across the toe line and mark back, normal and forward ball positions one ball-width apart. Keep stance width and target constant.','1. Hit the first set from the back marker, the second from normal and the third from forward.
2. Keep target, stance width and swing intention unchanged.
3. Record strike, start, curve and ground contact for every ball.
4. Return to the best position for the consolidation set.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Alignment stick; three ball-position markers; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-07','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the strike and low point task to be recognised.','1. Build posture and let the arms hang before placing the club behind the ball.
2. Measure hand-to-thigh spacing with the selected reference.
3. Make a half swing while maintaining arm radius through impact.
4. Step away and rebuild spacing before every ball.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-08','Place a small marker beside each foot so stance width can be rebuilt. Start with feet close enough to make the step or pressure shift obvious and use a short iron.','1. Begin with the feet close together or the trail foot on its marked start point.
2. Start the backswing, then make the prescribed step as the direction changes.
3. Let the step organise pressure and rotation before the arms accelerate.
4. Hit the ball and finish balanced, then blend the motion into a normal stance.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes strike and low point most predictably.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-09','Place a small marker beside each foot so stance width can be rebuilt. Start with feet close enough to make the step or pressure shift obvious and use a short iron.','1. Swing back slowly and pause before the backswing completes.
2. Move pressure back toward the lead side while the arms remain organised.
3. Pause again, then swing through at half speed.
4. Blend the two pauses into one continuous motion.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Club; balls; one foot-position marker','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-10','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the strike and low point task to be recognised.','1. Make a half swing and finish with chest turned, pressure on the lead foot and the body balanced.
2. Hold the finish for two seconds.
3. Repeat without adding speed or backswing length.
4. Progress to three-quarter swings while preserving the same finish.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-11','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the strike and low point task to be recognised.','1. Make a half backswing and pause.
2. Rehearse the trail shoulder moving down and forward as the pelvis and chest continue turning.
3. Hit a half shot and note where the club meets the ground.
4. Compare small changes in inclination rather than forcing the maximum range.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-12','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Make two slow rehearsals of short-backswing contact set using the selected forward of the ball task.
2. Hit the prescribed set (4 pairs + 6 transfer) at controlled speed.
3. Record strike and low point, strike and ball flight after each ball.
4. Finish with a no-aid set and compare it with the rehearsed set.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-13','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate forward of the ball of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Make two slow rehearsals of width-and-depth corridor using the selected forward of the ball task.
2. Hit the prescribed set (3 × 5 balls) at controlled speed.
3. Record strike and low point, strike and ball flight after each ball.
4. Finish with a no-aid set and compare it with the rehearsed set.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-14','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Make two slow rehearsals of transition-pump contact match using the selected forward of the ball task.
2. Hit the prescribed set (3 × (3 rehearsal + 3 balls)) at controlled speed.
3. Record strike and low point, strike and ball flight after each ball.
4. Finish with a no-aid set and compare it with the rehearsed set.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-15','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate forward of the ball of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Rehearse the hands through the marked delivery corridor without a ball.
