('DR-5-16','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the strike and low point task to be recognised.','1. Mark the intended delivery height with a soft visual reference beside the hands.
2. Make waist-high rehearsals returning the handle through that window.
3. Hit half shots while monitoring face strike and ground contact.
4. Remove the height reference and repeat the best pattern.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-17','Place a small marker beside each foot so stance width can be rebuilt. Start with feet close enough to make the step or pressure shift obvious and use a short iron.','1. Rehearse the selected pressure shift without a club.
2. Add the club and stop at a balanced half-swing finish.
3. Hit three balls using only the pressure cue, then three adding the pivot cue.
4. Keep the cue order that produces the most repeatable contact.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional strike and low point under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Club; balls; one foot-position marker','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-18','Choose a clear target, verify alignment and use the club named by the coach or a mid-iron. Start at a speed that allows the strike and low point task to be recognised.','1. Make three waist-high rehearsals with an early, middle and late face-reorientation feel.
2. Hit one ball with each feel at half speed.
3. Record start, curve and strike for each window.
4. Repeat only the window that produces the selected forward of the ball face delivery without losing contact.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Mid-iron; balls; ground line or strike mat','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-19','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Treat three consecutive balls as one set.
2. Rebuild the setup and task before every ball.
3. Score the set only after all three outcomes are known.
4. Restart the streak after a miss and continue until the stated success criterion is achieved.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional strike and low point under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Fade the rehearsal or physical reference, increase from half to three-quarter length, then retain the movement in a continuous no-aid swing.','Return to slow rehearsals and waist-high shots with a larger reference window before adding speed or swing length.'),
('DR-5-20','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Apply face spray and hit balls at controlled speed.
2. Check and mark strike after every ball.
3. Do not change the delivery variable until the required centre-strike count is reached.
4. Add the direction or low-point task while continuing to record strike.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-5-21','Build a generous gate with tees or sticks around the intended clubhead or hand route. Align the gate forward of the ball of the original pattern and leave enough room for an unforced first set.','1. Rehearse through the gate without a ball and identify the centre of the available space.
2. Hit at half speed without contacting either side.
3. Record gate success, strike and ball flight.
4. Narrow the gate slightly or remove one side for transfer; do not chase a perfect zero value.','Move through the centre of the available space with an unforced swing; the reference guides direction rather than becoming the target of a hit.','Two alignment sticks or four tees; balls; chosen club','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-5-22','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Make two slow rehearsals of sole-and-surface comparison using the selected forward of the ball task.
2. Hit the prescribed set (4 × 3 balls) at controlled speed.
3. Record strike and low point, strike and ball flight after each ball.
4. Finish with a no-aid set and compare it with the rehearsed set.','Observe and compare; do not try to manufacture a perfect result. Notice which condition changes strike and low point most predictably.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-5-23','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Swing until the lead arm is approximately parallel to the ground.
2. Turn through to a matching waist-high finish with steady rhythm.
