('DR-5-25','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Define one point each for functional strike, start/flight and the selected strike and low point window.
2. Hit every ball as a separate three-point challenge.
3. Record the score immediately without deleting poor shots.
4. Finish the full set and review which component loses the most points.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Reduce external feedback, narrow the success window and alternate clubs or targets while retaining strike and flight.','Use a half swing, a larger gate or clearer strike feedback until three consecutive contacts meet the basic standard.'),
('DR-5-26','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Treat three consecutive balls as one set.
