3. Score the set only after all three outcomes are known.
4. Restart the streak after a miss and continue until the stated success criterion is achieved.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional strike and low point under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-5-27','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Begin at roughly 60% effort and hit three balls.
