('DR-5-30','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Randomly call low, normal or high before each ball.
2. Change setup and finish length to create the trajectory while keeping the same strike standard.
3. Hit and score trajectory, face strike and ground contact.
4. Move to a different trajectory for the next ball.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional strike and low point under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-5-31','Place a small marker beside each foot so stance width can be rebuilt. Start with feet close enough to make the step or pressure shift obvious and use a short iron.','1. Mark a scoring corridor and one prohibited side.
2. Award points for target, functional corridor and preferred side; subtract for the prohibited miss.
3. Announce the score required before starting.
4. Complete the full set without technical resets or deleting shots.','Commit to the called task, accept the outcome and rebuild. The intention is functional strike and low point under changing demands, not a perfect rehearsal.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.'),
('DR-5-32','Draw or place a straight ground line perpendicular to the target. Put the ball on the line unless the drill specifies otherwise, apply face spray and use a mid-iron.','1. Hit the first ball with the trained task and record it.
2. After any miss, state the simple intention for the next shot rather than adding a new technical change.
3. Hit the recovery ball to the same task.
4. Score both overall retention and the ability to prevent two costly misses in sequence.','Sense the club reaching its lowest point on the target side of the ball while face strike and balance remain predictable.','Impact spray or face tape; ground line or towel; balls','Randomise target, club or trajectory, add a defined score and complete the task under a one-ball consequence format.','Return to a fixed target and predictable club, remove the score and complete one successful three-ball set before randomising again.')
) as content(code,setup,instructions,intention,equipment,progression,regression)
where item.code=content.code and item.item_type='golf_drill'
  and (item.setup,item.instructions,item.intention,item.equipment,item.progression,item.regression)
      is distinct from (content.setup,content.instructions,content.intention,content.equipment,content.progression,content.regression);

do $$
declare total integer; ready integer;
begin
  select count(*),count(*) filter(where instruction_complete) into total,ready from public.library_items where item_type='golf_drill';
  if total<>224 then raise exception 'Expected 224 golf drills, found %',total; end if;
  if ready<>224 then raise exception 'Expected 224 player-ready golf drills, found %',ready; end if;
end $$;
